{"ts": "2026-09-21T09:17:18.830581Z", "runId": "jev-guarded-20260921T120738", "label": "iter: --filter jev with the minimum-pool guard, paired haiku", "notes": "Same 12 cases as the unguarded run plus 3 new (cross/codex-sourced/negative). Isolating the shared 12: tool calls +3% -> -16%, cost -3% -> -10%, bytes -12% -> -9%, correctness 9->9 becomes 9->8. The 15-case correctness gain is baseline variance: the base arm went 2/3 -> 0/3 on the new cases between runs while the guard touches only the jev arm. review-sandbox-limits fails in both arms in both runs and is not discriminating.", "providers": "haiku", "suite": "jev-filter", "scope": "synthesis+decision+cross+negative", "artifacts": {"tool": "bce2f5fa5827", "skill": "563397af20e1", "provider": "f80369f4abf3", "cases": "177ff0f283e5", "git": "59bc0e3"}, "logs": "eval/results/logs/jev-guarded-20260921T120738", "detail": "eval/results/jev-filter.json", "gates": {"haiku": {"paired": 15, "repeats": 1, "sharedTwelve": {"calls": "+3% -> -16%", "cost": "-3% -> -10%", "bytes": "-12% -> -9%", "correct": "9->9 becomes 9->8"}, "clearsNoiseFloor": "cost and tool calls; correctness noise-dominated", "pass": false}}, "agg": {"session-grep": {"n": 15, "correct": 9, "graded": 15, "cost": 0.7076911, "toolCalls": 66, "toolResultChars": 284669, "acc": 0.6}, "session-grep-jev": {"n": 15, "correct": 10, "graded": 15, "cost": 0.5673138000000001, "toolCalls": 52, "toolResultChars": 214040, "acc": 0.667}}}
{"ts": "2026-09-21T09:51:21.009976Z", "runId": "jev-repeat3-20260921T122222", "label": "iter: --filter jev, 15 cases x 3 repeats, paired haiku", "notes": "Three repeats settle it. Correctness 36/45 vs 35/45 is no effect. Cost -10%, tool bytes -18%, tool calls -9% reproduce across repeats and are the real result. Six of fifteen cases are unstable across repeats in at least one arm (rpc-hardening-decision 0/3 base, sidebar-data-ownership 1/3 both, absent-deployment-target 1/3 vs 2/3, superset-mixup 2/3 vs 1/3, keywords-arc 3/3 vs 2/3, review-sandbox-limits 2/3 vs 1/3), so single-repeat correctness comparisons on this suite are not readable. review-sandbox-limits was rewritten first: its question did not say which review pass it meant and both arms correctly answered from 880044c1, where the feature WAS typechecked and driven live; it now scores 2/3 and 1/3 instead of 0/3. cross-codex-reviews is 3/3 in both arms, so filtering did not drop the second session it needs.", "providers": "haiku", "suite": "jev-filter", "scope": "synthesis+decision+cross+negative", "repeats": 3, "artifacts": {"tool": "bce2f5fa5827", "skill": "563397af20e1", "provider": "f80369f4abf3", "cases": "e9298f55ae8e", "git": "f816e3e"}, "logs": "eval/results/logs/jev-repeat3-20260921T122222", "detail": "eval/results/jev-filter.json", "gates": {"haiku": {"paired": 15, "repeats": 3, "passRate": "36/45 vs 35/45", "costRatio": 0.896, "charsRatio": 0.816, "callsRatio": 0.91, "unstableCases": "6/15", "clearsNoiseFloor": "efficiency only: cost -10%, bytes -18%, calls -9%; correctness no effect", "pass": false}}, "agg": {"session-grep-jev": {"n": 45, "correct": 35, "graded": 45, "cost": 2.0703096, "toolCalls": 203, "toolResultChars": 752653, "acc": 0.778}, "session-grep": {"n": 45, "correct": 36, "graded": 45, "cost": 2.3112751000000005, "toolCalls": 223, "toolResultChars": 921968, "acc": 0.8}}}
{"ts": "2026-09-21T12:21:51.767597Z", "runId": "naive-baseline-20260921T145940", "label": "baseline: naive-grep on the jev-filter case set, 15 cases x 3 repeats", "notes": "Naive measured alone so the two skill arms did not have to be re-run. Cost, bytes and calls compare across runs; correctness compares because the gap is far larger than this suite's resolution. Latency for the skill arms was lost to the results-file overwrite and is not recoverable, so only naive's 47.9s per run is recorded. Both skill arms were run with a prompt this session added (--candidates guidance and a grouped first search), so this is not a re-measurement of the historical session-grep arm.", "providers": "haiku", "suite": "jev-filter", "scope": "synthesis+decision+cross+negative", "repeats": 3, "artifacts": {"tool": "90993b9e6b6d", "provider": "ae789eda8dd0", "cases": "e9298f55ae8e", "git": "7c1e1ef"}, "logs": "eval/results/logs/naive-baseline-20260921T145940", "detail": "eval/results/iterations/naive-baseline-20260921T145940.json", "gates": {"haiku": {"paired": 15, "repeats": 3, "sessionGrepVsNaive": {"costRatio": 0.354, "charsRatio": 0.363, "acc": "0.8 vs 0.467"}, "jevVsNaive": {"costRatio": 0.317, "charsRatio": 0.296, "acc": "0.778 vs 0.467"}, "fiftyPercentCostGate": "both skill arms pass: 35% and 32% of naive cost at higher correctness", "pass": true}}, "agg": {"naive-grep": {"n": 45, "correct": 21, "graded": 45, "cost": 6.5296928, "toolCalls": 733, "toolResultChars": 2539589, "latencyMs": 2154940, "acc": 0.467}, "session-grep(prior run)": {"n": 45, "correct": 36, "cost": 2.3113, "toolCalls": 223, "toolResultChars": 921968, "acc": 0.8}, "session-grep-jev(prior run)": {"n": 45, "correct": 35, "cost": 2.0703, "toolCalls": 203, "toolResultChars": 752653, "acc": 0.778}}}
{"ts": "2026-09-22T07:50:41.043102Z", "runId": "floor-recheck-full-corpus-20260922T105041", "label": "recheck: relevance floor and minimum pool against the full configured corpus", "notes": "The original sweeps ran with SESSION_GREP_SOURCES_FILE unset, so the worktree used four default roots and never saw ~/.owner-operator/sessions and its 299 transcripts. Re-running the 15 verified-answer queries with the configured corpus pulled 49 of 289 candidates from that store, 17%. Both constants reproduce. Every verified answer is still inside the top-20 pool, none displaced by an oo session, and the lowest answer scored 0.89 against 0.82 before, so the 0.5 floor has more margin than first claimed. A floor of 0.7 still loses an answer once the 0.21 worst-case spread is counted. Median candidates dropped is still 0 at K<=8 and 1 at K=10, and wasted calls fell from 43% to 36% at K=10 and from 24% to 14% at K=20. Two gaps remain and are not fixed here: ~/.cursor/projects holds 36 transcripts with no adapter to read them, and the configured source list is narrower than the map owner-operator keeps at ~/.owner-operator/session_sources.json.", "providers": "none, jev scoring only", "suite": "floor-sweep", "scope": "15 verified-answer queries", "artifacts": {"tool": "5ea96357d0a6", "git": "69f6043"}, "gates": {"floor": {"candidates": 289, "answers": 15, "lowestAnswer": 0.89, "lostAt0.5": 0, "lostAt0.7WithVariance": 1, "medianDroppedK8": 0, "medianDroppedK10": 1, "verdict": "constants unchanged, evidence corrected", "pass": true}}}
